  "notes": "Official JBU plans index (catoid=33, 2025-2026 catalog, labeled Archived Catalog). Transcribed 2026-10-01 from the official PDF. Plan titled 'B.S. Criminal Justice' (College of Education and Social & Behavioral Sciences). No catalog year is printed inside the PDF; the official file name on the JBU plans index is 'Criminal Justice, B.S. Four-Year Plan 2025-2026', so catalog_year 2025-2026 is stamped honestly from the official file name, not invented. The plan prints two alternating row colors per year; the yellow rows form the odd-start sequence and the blue rows the even-start sequence. Footer preserved: 'This plan is only one possible arrangement. Speak to advisor about variations.' Footnote preserved: '*Bluefield College Course, but College looking for Adjunct to teach class on campus beginning Spring 2025' (attached to Corrections*).  This seed is the even-start sequence (Fall Even / Spring Odd rows). Genuine catalog discrepancies preserved: Sophomore Fall Odd prints 16 hours but the five listed courses sum to 15 (BIO 1003 3 + HST 2013 3 + BBL 2013 3 + POL 3253 3 + MTH1003 3); Sophomore Spring Even prints 15 hours but the five listed courses sum to 14 (HST 2023 3 + CRJ 4483 3 + CRJ 3233 3 + BBL 2022 2 + HST 2123 3). total_credits is the sequenced sum (120). Note the source prints two different Corrections course numbers across the variants: CRJ 3133 in the odd-start variant, CRJ 3113 here; kept as printed.\n\nallow_repeated_courses: the official JBU 'B.S. Criminal Justice' four-year plan (even-start sequence, catalog.jbu.edu catoid=33) prints PSY 1013 in freshman spring ('Introductory Psychology') and again in junior fall ('Introducion to Psychology' — JBU's own typo in the published plan); transcribed exactly as printed. This is the official source's own duplication, not a transcription error; no verifiable correction exists in any official JBU source, so the plan is preserved as printed. The official plan prints PSY 1013 Introductory Psychology in both Spring Odd of freshman year (term 2) and Fall Even of junior year (term 5) of the even-start sequence — a genuine duplication in JBU's published plan, sequenced exactly as printed (the junior-year listing carries JBU's own spelling 'Introducion to Psychology').",
